title: 'IO::K8s::List has to_json but no from_json -- last class outside the karr
  #59 symmetry'
updated: 2026-08-31T19:04:22Z
---

karr #59 made FROM_HASH inflate nested objects, so every class consuming
IO::K8s::Role::Resource is now to_json/from_json symmetric.
IO::K8s::List is not: it is a plain `use Moo` class that does NOT consume
the role.

Measured (post-#59):

  IO::K8s::List->does("IO::K8s::Role::Resource")  --> false
  ->can("to_json")   yes      ->can("TO_JSON")   yes
  ->can("from_json") NO       ->can("FROM_HASH") NO

It has its own to_json/TO_JSON, so it looks like a Resource from the
outside and then has no way back in. A caller who serializes a List and
tries to read it back hits "Can not locate object method from_json" --
after #59 that is the only class in the distribution behaving that way,
which makes it more surprising, not less.

Decision needed: consume the role (and check what the roles bring that
List must not have -- it is a container, not an API object with a GVK),
or state the asymmetry in POD as deliberate and point at
$k8s->inflate, which does handle List containers.

Note the List kinds were removed as API classes in 1.105 (see the *List
removal and IO::K8s::Deprecated); this ticket is about the generic
IO::K8s::List container that replaced them, not about those.

Found by the serialization lane while implementing karr #59 (verified by
the orchestrating agent).
Lane: decision first, then io-k8s-worker or io-k8s-doc-writer.

2026-08-31 03:50 Decision: bring List into the karr #59 symmetry rather than document the gap. Added hand-rolled from_json (decode UTF-8 -> FROM_STRUCT, optional $k8s) without consuming Role::Resource (which would break List's non-registry shape). Also made to_json byte-oriented (utf8=>1) per karr #53 so the pair round-trips non-ASCII. Fixed in bbf169fc, test t/61. Full suite green (4093); woven POD clean.
